{title: The Scribe's Life}
{subtitle: Jeremiah 36:1–4; 36:8–10; 36:23–26; 36:32; 45:1–5; 43:5–7}
{key: F}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [F] | [C/E] | [Dm] [Fmaj7/C] | [Bb] |
| [Csus4] [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]In [F]the fourth year [C/E]of King Jehoia[Dm]kim
[C]The [Bb]word of [C]the Lord came to Jeremi[F]ah
[C/E]He [Bb]called for Baruch son of [Am7]Neriah
[Dm]To write [Gm7]the words of the Lord on a [Csus4]scroll
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]As [F]Jeremiah dictat[C/E]ed the [Dm]words of the [Am]Lord
Ba[Bb]ruch wrote them down [C]with faithful [F]hands
[C/E]Through [Dm]the fire and [Am]the fear of the [Bb]king
[F/A]The [Gm7]scribe remained by the [C]prophet's [F]side [Fsus4]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]In the house of the [C/E]Lord at the New [Dm]Gate
[C][Bb]Baruch read [C]the words in the hearing [F]of all
[C/E]But the [Bb]king cut the [C7/Bb]scroll with a [Am7]knife [Dm7]
[Gm7]And threw the words into the [C]fire
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
As [F]Jeremiah dictat[C/E]ed the [Dm]words of the [Am]Lord
Ba[Bb]ruch wrote them down [C]with faithful [F]hands
[C/E]Through [Dm7]the fire and [Am]the fear of the [Bb]king
[F/A]The [Gm7]scribe remained by the [C]prophet's [F]side
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Dm7]You are seeking great [C]things for your[F]self [C/E]
[Dm7]Do not seek them [C]for I will bring [F]disaster
[C/E]But wher[Bb]ever you [C7/Bb]go I will [Am7]grant
[Dm7][Gm7]Your life as spoil in the [C]whole land
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]They went to [C/E]the land of E[Dm]gypt
[C6]Not [Gm7]obeying the [C]voice of the [F]Lord
{end_of_verse}
